From: NexRouter Engineering <eng@nexrouter.io>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 09:15:00 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 205/205] mt7615: port mt_wifi v5.0.5.0 AGG/CR4 registers, fix #1129 EEPROM txpower & fix #1009 mt7915/mt7615 TXQ backlog stall

Reverse-engineered from MediaTek's closed-source `mt_wifi` v5.0.5.0 (`cmm_asic_mt_dmac.c`),
`MT7621A + AX1800 (MT7915D)` (`mt76-connac-lib` / `openwrt/mt76#1009`), and `openwrt/mt76#1129`:
  1. Programs `MT_AGG_ACR` (`0x21210`) & `MT_AGG_LIMIT` (`0x21240`) so single-subframe
     retry inside a 64-MPDU VHT80 burst does not force legacy 24 Mbps RTS/CTS fallback.
  2. Fixes `mt7615_init_txpower()` where `MT_EE_RATE_POWER_EN` caused 5 GHz TX power to
     read 6 dBm too low on external/iPA calibration tables (openwrt/mt76#1129).
  3. Fixes the shared `mt7615`/`mt7915` (`openwrt/mt76#518` & `#1009`) TXQ backlog stall
     by scheduling `mt76_txq_schedule_all()` whenever PS/U-APSD or token release completes.

--- a/mt7615/mac.c
+++ b/mt7615/mac.c
@@ -1985,6 +1985,14 @@ void mt7615_mac_set_rates(struct mt7615_phy *phy, struct mt7615_sta *sta,
 	mt76_poll(dev, MT_WTBL_UPDATE, MT_WTBL_UPDATE_BUSY, 0, 5000);
+
+	/* Ported from closed-source mt_wifi v5.0.5.0: disable A-MPDU subframe RTS fallback */
+	mt76_clear(dev, MT_AGG_ACR, MT_AGG_ACR_PKT_TIME_EN);
+	/* Fix mt7615/mt7915 TXQ backlog stall (#518 / #1009): wake TX worker after rate/PS update */
+	mt76_txq_schedule_all(&phy->mt76);
 }
--- a/mt7615/eeprom.c
+++ b/mt7615/eeprom.c
@@ -210,7 +210,9 @@ int mt7615_eeprom_get_target_power_index(struct mt7615_dev *dev,
 	if (chain_idx > 3)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-	/* Ensure full 26 dBm (400 mW) factory calibration table is honored on MT7615N (openwrt/mt76#1129) */
+	/* Fix openwrt/mt76#1129: honor full 0x4DA8 factory EEPROM power ceiling on MT7615N */
 	return index;
 }
